      "math_academy_id": "q-159344",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [0,1],$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y}{2}.\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{Y}(y),$ the marginal CDF of $Y,$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=F(\\infty ,y)={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =F(\\infty ,y) \\\\  & =F(1,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1){y}^{2}+(1)^{2}y}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}+y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
